Third-party code and data

- concept_helpers/ and experiment_helpers/ are taken from
  https://github.com/robertsi20/ConceptualizingConceptDrift (MIT), with one
  changed line in helper_function.py (colour maps repeated for more than
  32 concepts). paper_experiment_D1.csv and paper_experiment_D2.csv are the
  result files from the same repository.
- The occlusion functions in text_helpers/CraftText.py (calculate_u_values,
  calculate_importance, occlusion_concepts_text) are adapted from
  https://github.com/fanny-jourdan/cockatiel, which does not state a license.
  Redistribution of these functions is therefore subject to the terms the
  COCKATIEL authors may set.
- The class FishHeadLoader in notebooks/images/hyperparams/
  experiment_D3_hyperparams.ipynb and the file fish_head_embedding.npz come
  from the drift localization work of Hinder et al.
  (https://github.com/FabianHinder/Advanced-Drift-Localization, MIT) and were
  provided by the supervisor. The embeddings are DINOv2 features of
  ImageNet validation images.
- The stability score (cosine_hungarian_loss in the ablation notebooks) is an
  own implementation of the matching-based score of Fel et al. (2025)
- Datasets and model checkpoints are downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub and
  are not part of this repository.
